*.sh text eol=lf

# `git diff --check` is a required gate (CI step "Reject trailing whitespace and
# blank lines at end of file"), and its default `blank-at-eol` rule reads a
# CommonMark hard line break — two spaces before the newline — as an error.
# Those spaces are content: they are what makes the header block of `TODO.md`
# and the `> **Versão:** … / > **Status:** …` front matter of every file under
# `docs/specs` render as separate lines instead of one run-on paragraph. There
# are about 180 of them across the specifications this wave's traceability
# cites, so the choice was between rewriting rendered documents to satisfy a
# whitespace preference and telling the gate which rule does not apply to prose.
# This is the second. `blank-at-eof` and `space-before-tab` stay on for Markdown
# — a stray blank line at the end of a document is still sloppiness, not a line
# break — and every other path keeps the full default rule set.
*.md whitespace=-blank-at-eol
